Since you have a GSDM, you might not need Magicbane for it's MR.
But, Magicbane absorbs most of the curses in the late game when
wielded. 
Cleaver requires two hands, and does decent damage.
If you want to use two-weapon combat or a shield of reflection,
Cleaver is not a good option. 

If you want a good weapon _right away_, a foolproof method would
be wishing for Frost Brand. Or, you just could sac until you get
Cleaver, then Stormy. Of course, you could wish for MB, then
sac until you get Cleaver, then hopefully Frost Brand...

I'm not sure if it's good to spend a wish for a fixed magical cloak,
but at least you'll find an elven cloak for MC. 

>Any particularily nasty monsters I should watch out for (like those
>pesty level draining vampires)?

(Master) Mind flayers, arch or master liches, disenchanters... 

You might want to read an instadeath spoiler at steelypips.org...

Monsters who cause delayed insta-deaths (or even insta-deaths)
usually provide you with a warning message, if you read them
all carefully. Example: "The kraken swings itself around you!"
Then you'll have at least one turn to figure out what to do about it.

